On the left, the region
<m>R = \{(r,\theta): a \le r \le b,\ \alpha\le\theta\le\beta\}</m>. On
the right, <m>R</m> divided into polar rectangles; the highlighted
polar rectangle <m>R_{ij}</m> has area
<m>\Delta A_i = r_i^*\,\Delta r\,\Delta\theta</m>, where
<m>(r_i^*, \theta_j^*)</m> is its center.
</caption>
