<p>
The subdivision of <m>R</m> into polar rectangles, and how the area of
a polar rectangle behaves as the grid is refined, is animated in
<xref ref="fig-polar-element-video"/>.
</p>

<figure xml:id="fig-polar-element-video">
<caption>
Animation of the polar area element. The region
<m>R = \{(r,\theta): 1 \le r \le 2,\ 0\le\theta\le\tfrac{\pi}{2}\}</m>
is divided into finer and finer polar rectangles; a highlighted cell
has area exactly <m>r^*\,\Delta r\,\Delta\theta</m>, and the sum
<m>\sum r^*\,\Delta r\,\Delta\theta</m> equals the area
<m>\tfrac{3\pi}{4}</m> of <m>R</m> at every stage.
</caption>
<video preview="play-button.png" xml:id="video-polar-element"
       source="videos/polar_area_element_1080p.mp4"
       width="70%" aspect="16:9"/>
</figure>

